&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Financial Systems Analyst II, Business Systems reports to the Senior Manager, Business Systems and is the technical owner on a lean, high-impact team. You will own the integration layer that connects SimpliSafe&#39;s financial and operational systems: NetSuite and Coupa at the&amp;nbsp;center, with a live network of retail, logistics, payments, and financial partners around them. This&amp;nbsp;is a builder&#39;s role. You will write the scripts, design the monitoring, automate what should be&amp;nbsp;automated, and use AI to improve how everything works. When something breaks, you find it&amp;nbsp;first and fix it. When there&#39;s a smarter way to build something, you build it. You will also share&amp;nbsp;technical ownership of Coupa and NetSuite administration, acting as the technical SME while&amp;nbsp;the primary admin handles day-to-day operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;● Own and develop integrations into, out of, and between NetSuite and Coupa, including&amp;nbsp;EDI and retail connectivity via SPS Commerce, banking and payments integrations,&amp;nbsp;freight invoice processing via Infios, and legal invoice routing via Brightflag&lt;br&gt;● Write and maintain custom NetSuite SuiteScript records (Scheduled Scripts, User Event&amp;nbsp;Scripts, Map/Reduce Scripts, RESTlets) to automate business logic, support data flows,&amp;nbsp;and handle integration error conditions&lt;br&gt;● Own the Grafana integration monitoring and alerting platform, respond to incidents in real&amp;nbsp;time, and continuously build out coverage to catch issues before users do&lt;br&gt;● Manage SSH and PGP keys for secure bank and financial partner file transfers, including&amp;nbsp;key rotation and partner coordination&lt;br&gt;● Serve as the technical SME for Coupa P2P and NetSuite, owning complex configurations&amp;nbsp;and integration issues as shared administrator alongside the primary admin&lt;br&gt;● Use AI tools to move faster and build better, and help shape how the Business Systems&amp;nbsp;team scales AI use across the function&lt;br&gt;● Partner with Finance (Accounting and AP), Logistics (supply planning, freight, fulfillment,&amp;nbsp;and manufacturing operations), and Retail (sales operations) on system initiatives and&amp;nbsp;escalations&lt;br&gt;● Find automation opportunities and build them; active work is already in progress with&amp;nbsp;more to come&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;● Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related technical field,&amp;nbsp;or equivalent professional experience&lt;br&gt;● 3 to 5 years in a technical business systems, ERP, or integration analyst role&lt;br&gt;● Solid JavaScript background required; NetSuite SuiteScript experience is a strong plus&lt;br&gt;● Experience managing integrations between enterprise systems via REST APIs or SFTP&lt;br&gt;● Ability to troubleshoot and resolve cross-system integration failures independently&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills, Abilities and Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;● NetSuite platform and SuiteScript experience; comfort with scripting languages generally&lt;br&gt;● Familiarity with EDI concepts and logistics data flows with retail and 3PL partners&amp;nbsp;preferred&lt;br&gt;● Experience with Coupa or a comparable P2P platform preferred&lt;br&gt;● Experience with Grafana, Datadog, or similar monitoring tools&lt;br&gt;● Strong diagnostic instincts; comfortable reading logs, tracing failures, and finding root&amp;nbsp;cause&lt;br&gt;● Clear communicator across technical and business teams&lt;br&gt;● Comfortable with reactive, iterative support work, not just structured projects&lt;br&gt;● Located in the Boston, MA area; hybrid with two core in-office days per week&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Values You’ll Share&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
