&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a senior, analytically-driven leader to own our Pricing &amp;amp; Promotions function. This is a player-coach role: you&#39;ll be hands-on with the work, manage and develop one direct report, and operate with significant autonomy and direct visibility to senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own our pricing/promotions experimentation program end-to-end, lead promotional strategy and performance analysis, and build out our discount budgeting capability. You&#39;ll also create and optimize a cross-functional pricing strategy, bringing a more coherent and intentional approach to how we price and discount across ecommerce, retail, and emerging channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end pricing/promotions testing roadmap — prioritize the backlog, design tests, set stakeholder expectations, analyze test results and drive rollout decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the promotional strategy, calendar and prioritization; partner with your direct report on execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop new promotional structures and ideas grounded in performance data and competitive intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize competitor analysis to inform our positioning and calendar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own stakeholder communication on promotions and test expectations across the business&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with finance and analytics teams to understand how promotional strategy impacts business performance, and make data-driven adjustments to achieve goals&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with acquisition team to identify opportunities to personalize promotions across channels in order to improve media performance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a leader in the adoption of AI-driven approaches for personalized promotions, leveraging models to optimize conversion rate and promotional spend efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own discount budgeting capability — track, model, and communicate promotional spend and ROI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use financial modeling to recommend promotional changes and evaluate their conversion and margin impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and develop one direct report, coaching them on analytical skills, business acumen, and stakeholder communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Required&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in growth, ecommerce, promotions, pricing, or a related analytical function — with a track record of owning experimentation and using data to drive business decisions; backgrounds in growth product management, lifecycle marketing, or pricing strategy are all strong fits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical background — you’re proficient with SQL and can independently design, analyze, and draw conclusions from A/B tests without relying on a data team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with promotional or marketing performance analysis, including financial modeling and conversion analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage and develop talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, structured communicator who can translate analytical findings into business recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating with autonomy and building structure in areas that are still maturing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
